{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/172904-generalized-siten-uzu-creation-rules","id":172904,"title":"Generalized 'Siten Uzu' Creation Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-18T09:37:47-07:00","id":172904,"title":"Generalized 'Siten Uzu' Creation Rules","content":"In <u>Skinchangers</u>,they present rules for the <i>Siten Uzu</i>, a creature created in a sort of reverse-Claiming process, effectively creating a Spirit-Claimed character with the human consciousness in control. However, the rules as presented are optimized for use with the Kitsune fox-spirits discussed in the book. Has anyone ever made an open source version of these rules, or do they still need to be created?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T10:41:02-07:00","id":172963,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, they still need to be created, however its rather easy to extrapolate between Skin-Changers and Predators. They essentially follow the Claimed rules, so the only trick is designing aspects for whichever spirit you'd rather use. I know it's taboo to mention, but Changing Breeds has a large, diverse list of aspects - they may require tweaking, but in my play-testing, they work out fine (the wonky mechanics are mostly in the Forms).<br /> <br /> Story wise, you do need a good reason for the spirit to 'hide inside' the human or otherwise let them be in control, rather than the ordinary form of Claiming. When I allowed a <i>siten uzu</i> in my game, we used a Raven spirit, and its reasoning for surrendering control was that it was trying to escape/hide from an enemy which would have been able to find it otherwise. I've also used a human cult which designed a ritual to subjugate spirits in this way; although there were control issues similar to Demon-Possessed, because the spirits were very not willing. Any motive similar to agreeing to be bound in a fetish could work out though.<br /> <br /> The old forums did have a character creation guide for <i>siten uzu </i>which clarified some of the rules rather well (though it still followed the kitsune assumption, as that's what the OP asked about). Penta's post toward the bottom was particularly helpful for me. Here it is in the archive: <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultbae2.html?g=posts&amp;t=69666\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/d...=posts&amp;t=69666</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T21:52:21-07:00","id":176730,"title":"","content":"I haven't gotten to the point of attempting to do much in the way of generalizing the template beyond merging the list of Aspects with the one from Predators, but I did think at some point that it might be interesting to see the various more obscure Celestines' &quot;wild-card&quot; status manifested in the occasional creation of living fetishes akin to the siten uzu; I had a fellow with a dormant Saturnian gaoler-Jaggling vaguely planned for a sample character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}